		"Quick Tutorial",
		"Blox Cards is a game of strategy and wits as you lead your combatants to victory!\n\nAt the start of a game, each player draws 7 cards and has 4000 Life. Use those cards to knock your opponent’s life to 0 to win!\n\nEvery turn phase you can either cast cards if you have the Studs to cast them. The first Coloured card in the beginning of your turn that you discard will generate and be sent to the Baseplate. Colourless cards cannot be discarded to the Baseplate, but can generate a Colourless stud. Subsequent discards will give you an additional generated stud for you to start casting powerful cards.\n\n\n"
	},
	{
		"Studs & Baseplate",
		"Cards cost Studs. There are two types of Studs: \n\n\\BColourless Studs (White) \n\\BColoured Studs (Red, Green, Blue, Yellow).\n\nWhen your turn ends, you lose all of your Coloured studs, then each fighter you have in play and each card in your Baseplate generates you a stud of its colour.\n\nLeft-click a card on your turn to cast it if you have enough studs. This’ll use up the Studs you have in the card’s cost.\n\nRight-click a card on your turn to discard it and gain a stud of that card’s colour. The first card discarded each turn goes to your Baseplate, and it’ll generate you more studs on the end of your turn. Try to only discard only once each turn to maximize baseplate generation!"
